From 32c2fae4fc046034900f2c7bbc16219e36a6b4ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: axeltlarsson <axel@arthro.ai>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:43:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add OSC 7501 program status.

Answer the OSC 7501 query and keep a pane's root record from program
status reports (rev 0.4) in the pane user options @ps_state, @ps_kind,
@ps_app and @ps_msg, so formats and hooks can show what a program such as
Claude Code is doing. The query reply goes through input_reply like the
DA1 reply, so it always arrives before the DA1 reply to the request a
program sends straight after the query.

A report is checked per the spec (pairs, limits, base64, UTF-8 without
control characters) and replaces the record; child records (with an id)
are checked and ignored. The pane-status-changed hook runs when the state
changes, with old_state and new_state. An OSC 133 prompt, a respawn or the
pane's process exiting drops an idle, working or blocked record, and RIS
drops any record.

The base64 and ASCII helpers follow autonomous-low-noise/tmux@4a77824.
---
