diff --git a/tmux.1 b/tmux.1
index b307484..40aa4af 100644
--- a/tmux.1
+++ b/tmux.1
@@ -6555,6 +6555,14 @@ Run when the terminal clipboard is set using the
 escape sequence.
 .It pane\-shell\-prompt
 Run when an OSC 133 shell prompt starts in a pane.
+.It pane\-status\-changed
+Run when a program reports a new state with OSC 7501.
+The old and new states are in the
+.Ql hook_old_state
+and
+.Ql hook_new_state
+formats; see
+.Sx PROGRAM STATUS .
 .It pane\-title\-changed
 Run when a pane title is changed.
 .It session\-closed
@@ -7858,6 +7866,35 @@ It can also be modified with the
 .Ic select\-pane
 .Fl T
 command.
+.Sh PROGRAM STATUS
+A program may report its state with the OSC 7501 program status escape
+sequence, and may first check for support by sending
+.Ql \e]7501\&;\&?
+followed by a primary device attributes request.
+.Nm
+answers the query and keeps the report without an id, the root record, in
+pane user options:
+.Bl -column "@ps_state" "Contents" -offset indent
+.It Sy "Option" Ta Sy "Contents"
+.It Li "@ps_state" Ta "idle, working, done, blocked or error"
+.It Li "@ps_kind" Ta "permission, question or auth when blocked"
+.It Li "@ps_app" Ta "the program's name"
+.It Li "@ps_msg" Ta "the program's message"
+.El
+.Pp
+Each report replaces the record and a report with state clear removes it.
+An OSC 133 shell prompt, a respawn or the pane's process exiting drops an
+idle, working or blocked record; a full reset drops any record.
+The
+.Ic pane-status-changed
+hook runs when the state changes.
+.Li @ps_msg
+is text from the program: formats should show it as a variable, for example
+.Ql #{q/h:@ps_msg} ,
+and never expand it again with
+.Ql E:\&
+or
+.Ql T:\& .
 .Sh GLOBAL AND SESSION ENVIRONMENT
 When the server is started,
 .Nm
diff --git a/tmux.h b/tmux.h
index b53dae8..95760fd 100644
--- a/tmux.h
+++ b/tmux.h
